 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.4.0] - 2026-11-15
+
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against the declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs.
+  Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` with an error message naming the failing property and constraint, allowing
+  the model to correct the call within the existing tool-round budget instead of failing the entire conversation.
+  A static tool's schema is compiled once at registration time; dynamic schemas compiled from function-valued
+  `ToolDefinitionSource` are cached by schema object. The validator is built with AJV and enforces `required` fields,
+  declared types, and `enum` constraints without coercion or defaults — extra properties pass through unchanged.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Migration:** An executor that relied on hand-validating its input now receives only input that has already passed
+  the declared schema. A tool that produced its own error message for malformed input will no longer see it. If your
+  tool validates proactively to produce a custom message, move that validation to your `inputSchema` or handle only
+  valid inputs. If you relied on seeing malformed input to produce an error, you now receive a `ToolResponse` instead
+  of an exception. The `ToolRegistry.execute` contract is stated in `specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md`.
+
